{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וכל העם ישמעו ויראו", :translit "v'khol ha'am yishm'u v'yira'u", :gloss "and all the people shall hear and fear"} {:he "אשימה עלי מלך", :translit "asimah alai melekh", :gloss "I shall set over me a king"} {:he "כל איש אשר ימרה את פיך", :translit "kol ish asher yamreh et pikha", :gloss "every man who rebels against your mouth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut: the phrase about hearing and fearing is adjacent to the parashah of appointing a king"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'וכל העם ישמעו ויראו' concludes the section on the authority of the supreme court (Deuteronomy 17:13). The very next verse opens the law of the king: 'כי תבא אל הארץ... ואמרת אשימה עלי מלך' (Deuteronomy 17:14). The rebel punished by the court is described with the phrase 'אשר ימרה את פיך' (Deuteronomy 17:12), and Ba'al HaTurim reads the adjacency as linking judicial authority to royal authority.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 17:12–14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולא יזידון עוד", :translit "v'lo yazidun od", :gloss "and they shall act presumptuously no more"} {:he "אשימה עלי מלך", :translit "asimah alai melekh", :gloss "I shall set over me a king"} {:he "להכרית מעיר ה' כל פועלי און", :translit "l'hakhrit me'ir Hashem kol po'alei aven", :gloss "to cut off from the city of YHWH all workers of iniquity"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut: the phrase about acting presumptuously no more is adjacent to the parashah of appointing a king"}], :frame {:text "David declares his purpose to destroy evildoers in Jerusalem: 'להכרית מעיר ה' כל פועלי און' (Psalms 101:8), in a psalm where he also speaks of governing with justice and destroying the wicked (Psalms 101:5–8). Ba'al HaTurim links the eradication of presumption ('yazidun') to the appointment of a king through David's words.", :sources ["Psalms 101:8" "Deuteronomy 17:14"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Smikhut: the phrase about hearing and fearing is adjacent to the parashah of appointing a king", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Smikhut: the phrase about acting presumptuously no more is adjacent to the parashah of appointing a king", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:37:11.270906423Z", :model "glm-5.2"}